While there is some overlap between spells and scrolls, there are a
lot of scrolls that have no spell and spells that have no scroll.  In
some cases they have similar names, but a scroll of fire and a fire
spell do very different things.  Overall, I'm pretty happy with the
game's choices about what to make available as scrolls or spells or
both.

None of which has anything to do with my post.  What you advocated
isn't the opposite of what I suggested, it's a completely different
issue.  Scrolls are different.  However, the correspondence between
wands and spells makes a lot of sense and I like it.  A wand for a
spell you have is like a number of "free" casts of the spell, but its
power and skill is fixed, rather than dependent on your knowledge and
experience.  I think it makes sense to have a wand for every spell
that you cast at a target or in a direction.

(I actually think there ought to be a way to *make* wands, out of
spells you know, but that's a whole different thread... :)

